# Direct dependencies of the resident Laya worker (python/worker.py).
#
# scripts/setup.sh compiles this file to python/requirements.txt with
# `uv pip compile` for Python 3.11 and installs the result into .venv, so the
# worker runs against exactly the versions this project was tested with.
#
# Pins are deliberate: `laya-mlx` is the native Apple MLX port of the Laya
# checkpoint and carries `mlx` itself, so there is no torch, transformers or
# tokenizer pin left to hold down. The Apple-only build is intentional: the
# compiled MLX wheels are macOS/arm64.
#
# `laya-mlx` needs huggingface_hub for snapshot resolution and tokenizers for
# the tokenizer, both of which it declares; the pins below only fix the
# versions this project was tested with.

laya-mlx==0.2.0
mlx==0.32.2
huggingface_hub==1.33.0
safetensors==0.8.0
tokenizers==0.23.2
numpy==2.4.6
